{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And it came between the camp. And it came</b> — the cloud — <b>between the camp of Egypt and between the camp of Israel, and it was</b> there <b>the cloud and the darkness.</b> And so it is written in Joshua: ״וישם מאפל ביניכם ובין המצרים״. ״And he illuminated the night״ — Rashi explained: the language of light. And if you ask: behold in Psalms, regarding ״ולילה אור בעדני״, Rashi explained it as the language of darkness — one may answer that the language of darkness refers to Egypt and the language of light refers to Israel, and the Targum proves it." "<b>And he illuminated the night.</b> The pillar of fire that went before them at night did not change its practice, and if it had gone behind them like the pillar of cloud, it would have illuminated for Egypt just as for Israel. But the cloud, which until now would sink down at evening, now stood behind them, and this matter caused Egypt not to approach Israel all night. Another interpretation: <b>and did not come near</b> — this one to that one: the pillar of fire did not come near to the pillar of cloud, for the one was before the camp of Israel and the one was before the camp of Egypt; but in the morning they came near and intermingled together before the camp of Egypt — and the strife, as explained further on."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "The last words והממום כמו שמפורש לקמן: reading uncertain; the word והממום (and the strife?) is obscure and possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:52.047222334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}